This is when the request, while maybe valuable in isolation, doesn't align with broader company or team goals or perhaps doesn't fit into your pre-established key priorities.

245
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:34,360
Right.

246
00:15:34,380 --> 00:15:37,850
It's not about capacity or expertise, but about strategic direction.

247
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:38,470
Exactly.

248
00:15:39,210 --> 00:15:41,230
Our source gives us strong phrases for this.

249
00:15:41,510 --> 00:15:48,060
You might say this new feature task, while important, doesn't align with my immediate sprint objectives.

250
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,440
Linking it to current defined goals.

251
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:50,720
Yes.

252
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:57,390
Or my manager and I have agreed on my key Q3 priorities and this new task isn't currently among them.

253
00:15:57,990 --> 00:15:59,630
